al numbers $(p,q,s).$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"57bb51e52373415853454469470ac7f3420ae9a438f582044b981e61b5f5e93b"},"seconds":52.20331883430481,"seed":85178179946828561,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the ordered triple \\((p, q, s)\\) for the circle equation \\(x^2 + y^2 - px - qy + s = 0\\) that passes through the vertices of the rectangle \\(ABCD\\) with opposite vertices \\(A = (3, 4)\\) and \\(C = (7, 10)\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Determine the center of the rectangle:**\n   The center of the rectangle (which is also the center of the circle) is the midpoint of \\(A\\) and \\(C\\). The midpoint formula is:\n   \\[\n   \\left( \\frac{x_1 + x_2}{2}, \\frac{y_1 + y_2}{2} \\right)\n   \\]\n   Substituting \\(A = (3, 4)\\) and \\(C = (7, 10)\\):\n   \\[\n   \\left( \\frac{3 + 7}{2}, \\frac{4 + 10}{2} \\right) = \\left( \\frac{10}{2}, \\frac{14}{2} \\right) = (5, 7)\n   \\]\n   So, the center of the circle is \\((5, 7)\\).\n\n2. **Determine the radius of the circle:**\n   The radius is the distance from the center to any vertex of the rectangle. We use the distance formula:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}\n   \\]\n   Using the center \\((5, 7)\\) and vertex \\(A = (3, 4)\\):\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{(5 - 3)^2 + (7 - 4)^2} = \\sqrt{2^2 + 3^2} = \\sqrt{4 + 9} = \\sqrt{13}\n   \\]\n   So, the radius of the circle is \\(\\sqrt{13}\\).\n\n3. **Write the equation of the circle:**\n   The standard form of the circle equation is:\n   \\[\n   (x - h)^2 + (y - k)^2 = r^2\n   \\]\n   where \\((h, k)\\) is the center and \\(r\\) is the radius. Substituting \\(h = 5\\), \\(k = 7\\), and \\(r = \\sqrt{13}\\):\n   \\[\n   (x - 5)^2 + (y - 7)^2 = 13\n   \\]\n\n4. **Convert the standard form to the general form:**\n   Expand the equation:\n   \\[\n   (x - 5)^2 + (y - 7)^2 = 13\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (x^2 - 10x + 25) + (y^2 - 14y + 49) = 13\n   \\]\n   Combine like terms:\n   \\[\n   x^2 + y^2 - 10x - 14y + 74 = 13\n   \\]\n   Move the constant term to the other side:\n   \\[\n   x^2 + y^2 - 10x - 14y + 61 = 0\n   \\]\n\n5. **Identify the coefficients \\(p\\), \\(q\\), and \\(s\\):**\n   Comparing with the general form \\(x^2 + y^2 - px - qy + s = 0\\), we have:\n   \\[\n   p = 10, \\quad q = 14, \\quad s = 61\n   \\]\n\nThus, the ordered triple \\((p, q, s)\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{(10, 14, 61)}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{(10, 14, 61)}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
